WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.950 --> 00:00:04.770
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

2
00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:06.070
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金赛。

3
00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:07.370
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演《办公室》。

4
00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:08.610
And we're best friends.
我们现在是最好的朋友。

5
00:00:08.710 --> 00:00:12.430
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.
我们正在为你们制作终极《办公室》重温播客。

6
00:00:12.590 --> 00:00:19.410
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.
每周，我们都会剖析一集《办公室》，并分享只有身临其境的我们才能告诉你的独家幕后故事。

7
00:00:19.590 --> 00:00:20.550
We're The Office ladies.
我们是《办公室》女士。

8
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:26.660
Da-na-na-na-na.
哒-那-那-那-那。

9
00:00:29.060 --> 00:00:30.180
Oh, Michael.
噢，迈克尔。

10
00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:31.180
Michael.
迈克尔。

11
00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:32.380
Bless his heart.
真可怜。

12
00:00:32.740 --> 00:00:35.940
You guys, today, it's employee transfer.
伙计们，今天我们要聊的是“员工调动”。

13
00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:43.000
It is Season 5, Episode 6, written by Anthony Farrell and directed by Dave Rogers.
这是第五季第六集，由安东尼·法瑞尔编剧，戴夫·罗杰斯执导。

14
00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:45.080
We have lots to say.
我们要聊的内容很多。

15
00:00:45.260 --> 00:00:46.920
There's a really good DVD commentary.
DVD评论音轨非常精彩。

16
00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:49.060
I didn't do any deep dives, though.
不过我这次没做深度挖掘。

17
00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:50.100
What?
什么？

18
00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:50.900
I'm sorry.
抱歉。

19
00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:52.840
In advance, for anyone who likes them.
提前向那些喜欢深度挖掘的听众道歉。

20
00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:55.680
And you're welcome, the people who hate them.
也欢迎那些讨厌深度挖掘的听众。

21
00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:57.340
I might need a minute.
我可能需要一点时间平复一下。

22
00:00:57.380 --> 00:00:58.320
No deep dives.
没有深度挖掘。

23
00:00:58.500 --> 00:00:59.400
I have a summary.
我有剧情梗概。

24
00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:04.960
I know you have a summary and fast facts, but we also reached out to a ton of people, so we have lots of good trivia.
我知道你有梗概和速览，但我们也联系了很多人，所以我们有很多精彩的幕后花絮。

25
00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:05.580
We did.
确实如此。

26
00:01:05.720 --> 00:01:06.640
That is very true.
非常正确。

27
00:01:07.180 --> 00:01:08.960
I will give you my summary.
我要开始讲梗概了。

28
00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:09.620
Do it.
请开始。

29
00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:14.880
Pam is embarrassed when no one else at corporate wears a costume on Halloween.
帕姆在万圣节穿了戏服，结果发现公司里其他人根本没穿，这让她非常尴尬。

30
00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:16.020
That is the worSt.
那真是太糟糕了。

31
00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:17.660
It was so funny.
那段太搞笑了。

32
00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:22.220
It was so funny to do, and it gets me every time.
拍的时候就很好笑，每次看我都忍不住笑。

33
00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:28.120
Holly and Michael deal with Holly's transfer to the Nashua branch.
霍莉和迈克尔要处理霍莉调往纳舒厄分部的事。

34
00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:32.660
Remember when David Wallace last week saw them kissing after the auction?
还记得上周大卫·华莱士看到他们在拍卖会后接吻吗？

35
00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:33.200
Yeah.
记得。

36
00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:34.160
Yeah.
记得。

37
00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:37.060
He was like, I'm not having another Jan and Michael on my hands.
他当时心想，我可不想再处理一次简和迈克尔那种烂摊子了。

38
00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:37.440
No.
没错。

39
00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:38.160
No depositions.
不需要再来一次取证了。

40
00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:39.860
Not on my watch.
绝不能在我的眼皮底下发生。

41
00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:40.180
No.
没错。

42
00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:44.460
Also, Dwight tries to get under Andy's skin by applying to Cornell.
此外，德怀特通过申请康奈尔大学来激怒安迪。

43
00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:45.960
I love that storyline.
我喜欢这条故事线。

44
00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:46.700
Same.
我也是。

45
00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:52.920
And finally, Pam is going to team up with Jim's brothers to play a prank on Jim.
最后，帕姆要和吉姆的兄弟们联手捉弄吉姆。

46
00:01:53.440 --> 00:01:55.920
Telling you those Halperts and the pranks.
我跟你说，这些哈珀特家族的人和他们的恶作剧。

47
00:01:56.120 --> 00:01:57.500
You know how I feel about pranks.
你知道我对恶作剧的态度。

48
00:01:57.580 --> 00:01:59.120
I know how you feel about them in real life.
我知道你在现实生活中对恶作剧的态度。

49
00:01:59.120 --> 00:02:01.240
The same as how I feel about tickling.
跟我对挠痒痒的态度一样。

50
00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:01.860
I know.
我知道。

51
00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:03.200
But Pam is like, sign me up.
但帕姆就像是说，算我一个。

52
00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:04.060
Let's prank away.
让我们开始恶作剧吧。

53
00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:04.620
I know.
我知道。

54
00:02:04.740 --> 00:02:05.580
Pam loves a prank.
帕姆很喜欢恶作剧。

55
00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:08.300
That's why Pam married Jim.
这就是帕姆嫁给吉姆的原因。

56
00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:08.940
That's right.
没错。

57
00:02:09.160 --> 00:02:10.280
Jenna would not marry Jim.
珍娜可不会嫁给吉姆。

58
00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:10.820
No.
不会。

59
00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:13.000
Because there'd be too much pranking.
因为恶作剧会太多了。

60
00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:15.700
All right.
好吧。

61
00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:17.600
Fast fact number one.
第一个小知识。

62
00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:19.140
New writer alert.
新编剧预警。

63
00:02:19.420 --> 00:02:20.520
Anthony Farrell.
安东尼·法瑞尔。

64
00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:20.920
Yeah.
没错。

65
00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:23.480
Anthony was with us for season five.
安东尼在第五季时加入了我们。

66
00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:25.500
He is a writer and a comedian.
他是一位编剧，也是一位喜剧演员。

67
00:02:25.880 --> 00:02:27.900
This was the first episode that he wrote for the show.
这是他为本剧编写的第一集。

68
00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:30.960
But I didn't know this until I looked it up.
但我查了资料才知道这一点。

69
00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:35.060
The first thing he wrote was actually the Kevin's Lone webisodes.
他写的第一部作品其实是《凯文的孤独》系列网剧。

70
00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:36.100
That's right.
没错。

71
00:02:36.220 --> 00:02:37.880
He wrote a series of webisodes.
他写了一系列网剧。

72
00:02:38.280 --> 00:02:40.780
And some of our writers got to break off and do that.
我们的一些编剧有机会分出来做那个。

73
00:02:40.940 --> 00:02:42.000
I would have loved to have done that.
我当时很想参与那个。

74
00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:43.480
I would have loved to have written a webisode.
我当时很想写一部网剧。

75
00:02:43.740 --> 00:02:46.300
I feel like you had a lot of freedom on the webisodes.
我觉得你在做网剧时有很大的自由度。

76
00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:47.240
Yeah, you did.
没错，确实有。

77
00:02:47.540 --> 00:02:48.440
They were pretty fun.
那些网剧挺有趣的。

78
00:02:48.540 --> 00:02:52.100
Which reminds me, we should break down the webisodes sometime.
这提醒了我，我们应该找时间拆解一下那些网剧。

79
00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:55.060
I mean, you don't even have to make it into a question.
我是说，你甚至不需要把它变成一个问题。

80
00:02:55.060 --> 00:02:56.240
We definitely should.
我们绝对应该这么做。

81
00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:58.520
The accountants, the webisodes won an Emmy.
会计师系列，那些网剧还拿过艾美奖。

82
00:02:58.740 --> 00:02:59.280
An Emmy.
艾美奖。

83
00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:02.080
I'm so jealous that you have an actual Emmy.
我真嫉妒你居然有一个真正的艾美奖奖杯。

84
00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:02.800
I know, lady.
我知道，女士。

85
00:03:02.900 --> 00:03:03.540
In your house.
就在你家里。

86
00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:04.040
I know.
我知道。

87
00:03:04.040 --> 00:03:05.680
Oh, it's very pointy.
噢，它非常尖。

88
00:03:06.020 --> 00:03:07.420
Yeah, those wings are pointy.
是啊，那些翅膀很尖。

89
00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:08.060
It's pointy.
它很尖。

90
00:03:08.680 --> 00:03:11.620
Angela, do you want to share that we got in touch with Anthony?
安吉拉，你想分享一下我们联系上安东尼的事吗？

91
00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:14.200
Yes, we were emailing with Anthony.
是的，我们一直在和安东尼发邮件。

92
00:03:14.380 --> 00:03:15.100
We had the wrong email.
我们之前的邮箱地址错了。

93
00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:16.640
Aaron Scherr to the rescue.
多亏了亚伦·谢尔出手相救。

94
00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:17.500
Thank you, Aaron.
谢谢你，亚伦。

95
00:03:17.640 --> 00:03:18.320
Thank you, Aaron.
谢谢你，亚伦。

96
00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:19.120
Got us in touch.
帮我们联系上了他。

97
00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:20.920
It was so great to reconnect with him.
能和他重新取得联系真是太棒了。

98
00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:24.040
He and his family are back in Toronto, where he's from.
他和家人回到了多伦多，那是他的家乡。

99
00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:25.300
And they're doing awesome.
他们现在过得非常好。

100
00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:28.860
He shared with me that he is the showrunner for a show called
他告诉我，他现在是一部剧的剧集主管，剧名叫

101
00:03:28.860 --> 00:03:31.700
The Parker Andersons slash Amelia Parker.
《帕克·安德森一家》和《阿米莉亚·帕克》。

102
00:03:31.700 --> 00:03:36.220
And it's actually two shows about the same characters from two different perspectives.
其实这是两部关于同一批角色、但视角不同的剧集。

103
00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:37.580
I love that.
我喜欢这个设定。

104
00:03:37.780 --> 00:03:38.600
It's so cool.
太酷了。

105
00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:40.260
He shared a lot of stuff with us.
他跟我们分享了很多内容。

106
00:03:40.340 --> 00:03:41.580
We're going to sprinkle it through the episode.
我们会在这一集中穿插介绍。

107
00:03:41.720 --> 00:03:45.720
But one of the things he said was, before he got the office, he was a comedian,
但他提到的一件事是，在进入《办公室》剧组之前，他是一名喜剧演员，

108
00:03:45.720 --> 00:03:47.400
but he still needed that day job.
但他仍然需要一份日常工作。

109
00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:50.920
And he was working at Countrywide Home Loans.
当时他在全美房屋贷款公司工作。

110
00:03:51.640 --> 00:03:55.960
And he was so excited when he got the job as writer on the office,
当他得到《办公室》编剧这份工作时，他非常兴奋，

111
00:03:55.960 --> 00:03:58.800
because it meant he could quit Countrywide Home Loans.
因为这意味着他可以辞掉全美房屋贷款公司的工作了。

112
00:03:58.980 --> 00:04:03.100
He quit like the day before he started in the writer's room, right?
他好像是在进编剧室的前一天辞职的，对吧？

113
00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:03.700
Yeah, he was working.
是的，他当时还在上班。

114
00:04:03.700 --> 00:04:04.060
Something crazy.
简直不可思议。

115
00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:06.180
Yeah, he was working at Countrywide Home Loans.
没错，他当时就在全美房屋贷款公司工作。

116
00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:09.640
And then literally like the next day, he was like, I'm going to go right now on a TV show.
然后就在第二天，他就像是说，我现在要去拍电视剧了。

117
00:04:09.640 --> 00:04:15.540
But all of that experience paid off because he was often called on in the writer's room to pitch
但所有的这些经历都派上了用场，因为在编剧室里，他经常被要求构思

118
00:04:15.540 --> 00:04:19.800
like those very minutiae office space storylines.
那些非常琐碎的办公室职场剧情。

119
00:04:20.040 --> 00:04:21.860
And he sent us in audio clips.
他还给我们发来了音频片段。

120
00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:24.120
We'll share those and some other trivia he gave us.
我们会分享这些片段以及他提供的其他一些花絮。

121
00:04:24.280 --> 00:04:29.960
It's interesting because actually not a lot of our writers had real office work experience.
很有意思，因为实际上我们很多编剧并没有真正的办公室工作经验。

122
00:04:29.960 --> 00:04:31.700
So he was a find.
所以他是个难得的人才。

123
00:04:31.900 --> 00:04:34.040
This was awesome to have him in there.
有他在真是太棒了。

124
00:04:34.360 --> 00:04:34.860
Great perspective.
视角很独特。

125
00:04:34.860 --> 00:04:39.620
All right, fast fact number two, new director alert.
好了，第二个速览事实，新导演预警。

126
00:04:39.980 --> 00:04:42.540
Yes, our very own Dave Rogers.
没错，就是我们自己的戴夫·罗杰斯。

127
00:04:42.940 --> 00:04:43.600
Our editor.
我们的剪辑师。

128
00:04:43.940 --> 00:04:44.180
Yeah.
是的。

129
00:04:44.460 --> 00:04:48.320
If you guys haven't listened to his extended interview in our revisited episode,
如果你们还没听过他在我们回顾集里的深度访谈，

130
00:04:48.320 --> 00:04:52.660
you should check it out because he is an amazing person and knows so much about the show.
你们一定要去听听，因为他是一个了不起的人，而且对这部剧了解得非常透彻。

131
00:04:52.860 --> 00:04:56.900
I dare say, I don't know if anyone else knows the show as well as him.
我敢说，我不知道还有谁能像他一样了解这部剧。

132
00:04:57.080 --> 00:04:58.320
You should dare to say that.
你应该敢说出来。

133
00:04:58.320 --> 00:04:59.260
I dare say it then.
那我就敢说了。

134
00:04:59.440 --> 00:04:59.820
Say it.
说吧。

135
00:04:59.900 --> 00:05:00.620
I dare say it.
我敢说。

136
00:05:00.680 --> 00:05:01.320
She said it.
她说出来了。

137
00:05:01.380 --> 00:05:01.860
I said it.
我说出来了。

138
00:05:01.860 --> 00:05:04.360
We were also able to get in touch with Dave.
我们也联系上了戴夫。

139
00:05:04.620 --> 00:05:08.940
He shared with me that he was so nervous to direct.
他跟我分享说，他当时对执导感到非常紧张。

140
00:05:09.140 --> 00:05:11.260
Very excited, but he had a ton of anxiety.
非常兴奋，但也充满了焦虑。

141
00:05:11.480 --> 00:05:17.680
He said he had a panic attack the night before filming, but he just pushed through.
他说他在拍摄前一天晚上甚至惊恐发作了，但他还是坚持了下来。

142
00:05:17.940 --> 00:05:24.280
I was really curious like what the most challenging thing was coming from editing and then directing.
我真的很好奇，从剪辑转行做导演，最具挑战性的事情是什么。

143
00:05:24.600 --> 00:05:25.540
Oh, that's a good question.
哦，这是个好问题。

144
00:05:25.740 --> 00:05:29.120
He said the toughest thing about this episode was that there were so many locations.
他说这一集最难的地方在于场景太多了。

145
00:05:29.120 --> 00:05:32.120
There were these multiple storylines.
有这么多条故事线。

146
00:05:32.540 --> 00:05:36.040
Michael had this huge emotional journey to go on.
迈克尔要经历一段巨大的情感历程。

147
00:05:36.300 --> 00:05:36.460
Yeah.
是的。

148
00:05:36.680 --> 00:05:37.900
And a physical journey.
还有一段身体上的旅程。

149
00:05:38.240 --> 00:05:38.840
Yes.
没错。

150
00:05:39.040 --> 00:05:43.600
He said that the most challenging thing for him was just the pace of shooting.
他说对他来说最具挑战性的就是拍摄的节奏。

151
00:05:44.540 --> 00:05:50.320
He said there's one thing if you have a ton of scenes in the bullpen and you have to make your day,
他说，如果你在办公区有很多场戏要拍，而且必须在一天内完成，那是一回事，

152
00:05:50.380 --> 00:06:02.700
but it's a whole other thing if after you finish a scene you have to pick up the entire crew and all the gear and move to another place and reset up because that eats up so much of your on-camera shoot time.
但如果你拍完一场戏后，还得带着整个剧组和所有设备转移到另一个地方重新布置，那就是另一回事了，因为那会占用大量拍摄时间。

153
00:06:02.700 --> 00:06:12.140
Yeah, but he did feel that coming from editing gave him an advantage because he just knew inherently the kind of stuff that got used on the show.
没错，但他确实觉得剪辑出身让他占了优势，因为他天生就知道什么样的素材会被用在节目里。

154
00:06:12.320 --> 00:06:17.720
He had watched so many directors do shots that were just never going to make it in.
他看过太多导演拍的镜头根本就进不了最终成片。

155
00:06:18.080 --> 00:06:21.260
So he said he was able to be really, really efficient.
所以他说他能够做到非常、非常高效。

156
00:06:21.760 --> 00:06:23.680
And he got to edit this episode.
而且他还亲自剪辑了这一集。

157
00:06:23.900 --> 00:06:28.360
Oh, that's great because how hard would it be as an editor to then direct and then give it away?
噢，那太棒了，因为作为剪辑师，拍完之后再把片子交给别人剪，那得多难受啊？

158
00:06:28.580 --> 00:06:29.400
I know, right?
可不是嘛，对吧？

159
00:06:29.400 --> 00:06:30.460
Yeah, I would think.
是啊，我也这么想。

160
00:06:30.640 --> 00:06:36.980
He said that Dean Holland assembled a few scenes and then Dave took over and he did a full assembly.
他说迪恩·霍兰德剪辑了几个场景，然后戴夫接手完成了全片的初剪。

161
00:06:36.980 --> 00:06:40.660
He did like a director's cut and he said not much changed.
他做了一个导演剪辑版，他说改动并不大。

162
00:06:40.880 --> 00:06:41.720
I doubt it.
我表示怀疑。

163
00:06:41.860 --> 00:06:46.980
And he was really, really proud that basically it was his director's cut that went to air.
他非常、非常自豪，因为基本上就是他的导演剪辑版播出的。

164
00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:47.740
Nice.
不错。

165
00:06:48.020 --> 00:06:51.000
Well, I have more stuff from Dave too, so you can share that.
好吧，我还有更多关于戴夫的内容，你可以分享一下。

166
00:06:51.400 --> 00:06:55.600
My fast fact number three is fun facts about Nashua.
我的第三个速览事实是关于纳舒厄的趣事。

167
00:06:56.040 --> 00:06:56.900
Let's hear them.
说来听听。

168
00:06:56.900 --> 00:06:59.360
I mean, Holly has to go live in Nashua.
我是说，霍莉得去纳舒厄生活。

169
00:06:59.480 --> 00:07:00.700
Don't we want to know more about it?
难道我们不想多了解一下那里吗？

170
00:07:00.760 --> 00:07:01.220
I do.
我想。

171
00:07:01.640 --> 00:07:02.040
Good.
很好。

172
00:07:02.420 --> 00:07:03.720
I'm going to tell you.
那我就告诉你。

173
00:07:03.860 --> 00:07:04.120
Okay.
好的。

174
00:07:04.720 --> 00:07:13.600
Holly is lucky because Nashua was named the best place to live in America two times in an annual survey by Money Magazine.
霍莉很幸运，因为纳舒厄曾在《金钱》杂志的年度调查中两次被评为全美最佳居住地。

175
00:07:13.600 --> 00:07:17.560
And it is the only city to ever win that ranking twice.
而且它是唯一一个两次获得该排名的城市。

176
00:07:17.940 --> 00:07:19.400
Holy crap, Nashua.
天哪，纳舒厄。

177
00:07:19.700 --> 00:07:22.400
It was in 1987 and 1998.
那是在1987年和1998年。

178
00:07:22.740 --> 00:07:24.720
Going strong at the end of the 90s.
90年代末势头很猛啊。

179
00:07:24.880 --> 00:07:25.160
Really?
真的吗？

180
00:07:25.160 --> 00:07:26.300
What else you got?
你还有什么？

181
00:07:26.580 --> 00:07:27.420
Russian dressing.
俄罗斯沙拉酱。

182
00:07:28.320 --> 00:07:29.740
Originated in Nashua?
起源于纳舒厄？

183
00:07:29.900 --> 00:07:30.100
Yeah.
对。

184
00:07:30.380 --> 00:07:31.180
The salad dressing.
就是那种沙拉酱。

185
00:07:31.320 --> 00:07:31.900
Russian dressing.
俄罗斯沙拉酱。

186
00:07:32.200 --> 00:07:32.440
No.
不会吧。

187
00:07:32.660 --> 00:07:32.960
What?
什么？

188
00:07:33.060 --> 00:07:34.580
You said you didn't have any deep dives.
你之前说你没有深度挖掘的内容。

189
00:07:34.640 --> 00:07:35.320
You were fooling.
你在骗人。

190
00:07:35.600 --> 00:07:38.080
This is a mini deep dive on Nashua.
这算是对纳舒厄的一次小型深度挖掘。

191
00:07:38.420 --> 00:07:38.800
Okay.
好吧。

192
00:07:38.820 --> 00:07:39.200
You're right.
你说得对。

193
00:07:39.280 --> 00:07:39.980
It kind of is.
确实算得上。

194
00:07:40.100 --> 00:07:41.560
And also on Russian dressing.
还有关于俄罗斯沙拉酱的。

195
00:07:41.780 --> 00:07:45.620
It was created by a grocer named James Colburn.
它是由一位名叫詹姆斯·科尔伯恩的杂货商发明的。

196
00:07:45.820 --> 00:07:47.380
He started mixing it up.
他开始尝试调制这种酱料。

197
00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:49.880
It looks like around 1910.
看起来大约是在1910年左右。

198
00:07:50.120 --> 00:07:50.520
Okay.
好的。

199
00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:56.320
And he started selling it at his grocery store under the name Colburn's Mayonnaise Salad Dressing.
他开始在自己的杂货店里以“科尔伯恩蛋黄酱沙拉酱”的名字出售。

200
00:07:56.680 --> 00:08:00.360
Well, that's not a catchy title, so I can see why they had to zhuzh it up.
嗯，那名字可真不吸引人，所以我明白为什么他们得给它润色一下了。

201
00:08:00.620 --> 00:08:05.920
Soon, he started manufacturing it on a bigger scale and shipping it around to other places.
很快，他开始大规模生产并将其运往其他地方销售。

202
00:08:05.920 --> 00:08:12.720
And he got so rich that he was able to retire in 1924.
他变得非常富有，以至于在1924年就能退休了。

203
00:08:13.300 --> 00:08:13.780
Wow.
哇。

204
00:08:14.060 --> 00:08:16.700
So just 14 years of selling this salad dressing.
所以只卖了14年的沙拉酱。

205
00:08:16.840 --> 00:08:18.820
And he was like, peace out.
他就直接说，拜拜了您嘞。

206
00:08:19.120 --> 00:08:20.440
Should we make a salad dressing?
我们要不要也做一款沙拉酱？

207
00:08:20.860 --> 00:08:22.060
What's our salad dressing?
我们的沙拉酱会是什么样的？

208
00:08:22.200 --> 00:08:23.180
What would be in it?
里面会放什么呢？

209
00:08:23.480 --> 00:08:25.780
What do you like in a salad dressing, lady?
女士，你喜欢沙拉酱里有什么？

210
00:08:26.080 --> 00:08:27.360
Well, you had me at mayonnaise.
嗯，你提到蛋黄酱我就心动了。

211
00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:28.440
Okay.
好吧。

212
00:08:28.680 --> 00:08:31.940
So we'll do some kind of mayo-based salad dressing.
那我们就做一种以蛋黄酱为基底的沙拉酱。

213
00:08:32.780 --> 00:08:33.940
I also like lemon.
我还喜欢柠檬。

214
00:08:34.220 --> 00:08:35.040
Do those mix?
这两样能混在一起吗？

215
00:08:35.140 --> 00:08:35.540
I don't know.
我不知道。

216
00:08:35.680 --> 00:08:38.800
I don't know, because I was going to say maybe like a spicy mustard.
我不知道，因为我本来想说也许可以加点辣芥末。

217
00:08:39.080 --> 00:08:39.460
Oh.
哦。

218
00:08:39.780 --> 00:08:45.140
Because I know they do a honey mustard salad dressing, but has anyone paired a spicy mustard with a mayo yet?
因为我知道有蜂蜜芥末沙拉酱，但有人把辣芥末和蛋黄酱搭配过吗？

219
00:08:45.460 --> 00:08:45.900
Probably.
应该有吧。

220
00:08:46.120 --> 00:08:47.100
We need to cut this out.
我们得把这段剪掉。

221
00:08:47.220 --> 00:08:49.420
We need to cut this out because we're onto something.
我们得把这段剪掉，因为我们好像发现了什么商机。

222
00:08:49.940 --> 00:08:54.500
And we'll never do it, and someone else will, and then we'll be mad for the rest of our lives.
如果我们不去行动，别人做了，我们余生都会后悔的。

223
00:08:54.500 --> 00:08:58.180
Office ladies, but we need to give it a really long, clunky name.
办公室女士，但我们得给它起个又长又拗口的名字。

224
00:08:58.500 --> 00:09:02.180
Office ladies, creamy mayonnaise, spicy mustard delight.
办公室女士，奶油蛋黄酱，辣芥末之悦。

225
00:09:02.780 --> 00:09:03.120
Yes.
没错。

226
00:09:03.520 --> 00:09:04.540
And then later-
然后以后——

227
00:09:04.540 --> 00:09:05.340
Delight's got to go on the end.
“之悦”必须放在最后。

228
00:09:05.460 --> 00:09:06.440
I don't care what it is.
我不在乎它叫什么。

229
00:09:06.580 --> 00:09:08.880
Later, we'll call it like Dutch dressing.
以后，我们就叫它荷兰酱之类的。

230
00:09:09.120 --> 00:09:10.400
We'll just pick a country.
我们随便选个国家就行。

231
00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:11.960
Denmark dressing.
丹麦酱。

232
00:09:12.220 --> 00:09:13.340
We'll just pick a random country?
我们就随便选个国家？

233
00:09:13.340 --> 00:09:14.040
Pick a country.
选个国家吧。

234
00:09:14.240 --> 00:09:14.460
Okay.
好吧。

235
00:09:14.720 --> 00:09:15.720
This is the formula.
这就是配方。

236
00:09:16.020 --> 00:09:16.380
Oh, okay.
哦，好吧。

237
00:09:16.540 --> 00:09:18.520
And then we'll retire in 14 years.
然后我们14年后退休。

238
00:09:18.840 --> 00:09:18.920
Okay.
好的。

239
00:09:19.640 --> 00:09:20.040
All right.
行吧。

240
00:09:20.040 --> 00:09:27.520
My final fun fact about Nashua is also about Amy Ryan, her character in Gone Baby Gone.
关于纳舒厄的最后一个趣事也和艾米·瑞安有关，是她在《失踪宝贝》里的角色。

241
00:09:27.720 --> 00:09:27.940
Yeah.
嗯。

242
00:09:28.300 --> 00:09:30.060
She is being interrogated-
她当时正在接受审讯——

243
00:09:30.060 --> 00:09:30.320
Yeah.
嗯。

244
00:09:30.720 --> 00:09:32.560
About a possible drug deal.
关于一次可能的毒品交易。

245
00:09:32.800 --> 00:09:33.000
Yeah.
嗯。

246
00:09:33.400 --> 00:09:38.300
