我会去买的。

320
00:12:25.220 --> 00:12:25.960
We'll be right back.
我们马上回来。

321
00:12:26.280 --> 00:12:37.120
All right.
好的。

322
00:12:37.180 --> 00:12:37.840
We are back.
我们回来了。

323
00:12:37.860 --> 00:12:40.120
And you guys, it is Halloween at Dunder Mifflin.
伙计们，邓德·米福林公司迎来万圣节了。

324
00:12:40.120 --> 00:12:40.900
It sure is.
确实如此。

325
00:12:40.900 --> 00:12:42.640
This is our Halloween cold open.
这是我们的万圣节开场戏。

326
00:12:42.880 --> 00:12:45.460
Not through the rest of the episode, just in the cold open.
并不是整集都是，只是开场戏而已。

327
00:12:45.700 --> 00:12:47.060
Well, we found out why.
嗯，我们找到了原因。

328
00:12:47.280 --> 00:12:48.780
Let's play Anthony's first clip.
让我们播放安东尼的第一段剪辑。

329
00:12:48.940 --> 00:12:49.860
He talks all about it.
他讲了所有相关内容。

330
00:12:50.040 --> 00:12:53.600
The show was initially, the entire episode was supposed to be Halloween.
最初，整集节目都设定为万圣节主题。

331
00:12:53.880 --> 00:12:55.900
So everyone was in their costumes for the entire episode.
所以每个人在整集里都穿着戏服。

332
00:12:56.040 --> 00:12:57.220
So Andy was a kitten initially.
安迪最初扮的是小猫。

333
00:12:57.220 --> 00:13:04.040
I think, and the whole B story with Dwight being in the Cornell sweater, that was his
我想，还有德怀特穿着康奈尔大学毛衣的那条副线，那是他的

334
00:13:04.040 --> 00:13:06.180
costume, an accidental costume initially.
戏服，最初是一次意外的装扮。

335
00:13:06.600 --> 00:13:08.280
And that's where that story came from.
那个故事就是这么来的。

336
00:13:08.480 --> 00:13:13.580
So costume wise, we had a thing where once we decided we were going to just put the Halloween
关于戏服，我们当时决定只把万圣节

337
00:13:13.580 --> 00:13:16.960
stuff in the cold open, we rewrote the cold open.
内容放在开场戏里，于是我们重写了开场戏。

338
00:13:17.040 --> 00:13:18.980
And that was mostly led by Lee and Gene.
这主要是由李和吉恩主导的。

339
00:13:19.140 --> 00:13:22.780
And that's where the idea for the three jokers came from.
三个小丑的点子就是这么来的。

340
00:13:22.780 --> 00:13:28.700
That was obviously a situation that year with that costume being super popular.
那一年那个装扮超级流行，这显然是个热门话题。

341
00:13:29.380 --> 00:13:32.240
And they just totally made the most of that situation.
他们充分利用了那个情况。

342
00:13:32.240 --> 00:13:33.140
It was amazing.
太棒了。

343
00:13:33.280 --> 00:13:37.460
The Charlie Chaplin thing, that was actually a full runner for you, Jenna.
查理·卓别林的那个梗，其实原本是为你准备的完整桥段，珍娜。

344
00:13:37.600 --> 00:13:41.300
We had initially in the first draft where you were going to be, it was Halloween all
在初稿里，我们原本设定是万圣节

345
00:13:41.300 --> 00:13:41.440
day.
一整天。

346
00:13:41.540 --> 00:13:44.720
So it was just going to be you running around the New York office as the only person dressed
所以原本是你一个人在纽约办公室里跑来跑去，是唯一一个

347
00:13:44.720 --> 00:13:46.740
for Halloween, trying not to look like Hitler.
穿着万圣节服装的人，还要努力让自己看起来不像希特勒。

348
00:13:47.240 --> 00:13:48.860
And it was a fun little runner for you.
那对你来说是个很有趣的小桥段。

349
00:13:48.940 --> 00:13:52.980
But I think the story we got eventually with Jim's brothers and that beautiful thing with,
但我认为我们最终呈现的故事，关于吉姆的兄弟们，还有那段美好的情节，

350
00:13:53.140 --> 00:13:58.120
you know, you taking the heat like that around them and having that nice little moment.
你知道，你替他们承担了压力，并有了那个温馨的小时刻。

351
00:13:58.240 --> 00:14:00.640
I think that that to me felt more right.
我觉得那样对我来说感觉更对味。

352
00:14:00.760 --> 00:14:02.520
And I love that we ended up going there with the story.
而且我很喜欢我们最终让故事走向那个方向。

353
00:14:03.480 --> 00:14:06.200
Yeah, it was going to be a whole Halloween episode.
是啊，本来打算拍成一整集万圣节特辑的。

354
00:14:06.200 --> 00:14:07.440
And then they changed it up.
后来他们改了主意。

355
00:14:07.820 --> 00:14:08.120
Yes.
没错。

356
00:14:08.420 --> 00:14:13.020
Anthony shared in the DVD that all those Halloween costumes would actually be distracting from
安东尼在DVD里分享说，所有那些万圣节服装其实会分散观众对

357
00:14:13.020 --> 00:14:14.160
all the other storylines.
其他剧情线的注意力。

358
00:14:14.260 --> 00:14:15.920
So they just made it the cold open.
所以他们干脆把它改成了开场戏。

359
00:14:15.920 --> 00:14:18.340
And I have a costume breakdown.
我这里有一份服装清单。

360
00:14:18.580 --> 00:14:19.080
Oh, good.
哦，太好了。

361
00:14:19.180 --> 00:14:21.440
Because I have some good details about some of the costumes.
因为我有一些关于这些服装的精彩细节。

362
00:14:21.580 --> 00:14:21.880
Okay.
好的。

363
00:14:22.120 --> 00:14:23.260
What's everyone wearing, Angela?
大家都穿了什么，安吉拉？

364
00:14:23.400 --> 00:14:26.000
So we have the scripts thanks to Jamesopedia.
多亏了Jamesopedia，我们拿到了剧本。

365
00:14:26.560 --> 00:14:28.880
So per the script, here are some details.
根据剧本，这里有一些细节。

366
00:14:29.660 --> 00:14:34.600
Stanley, in the script it says, is wearing a creature from the Black Lagoon rubber mask
剧本里写着，斯坦利戴着一个黑湖妖的橡胶面具，

367
00:14:34.600 --> 00:14:36.420
with his regular suit.
身上穿着他平时的西装。

368
00:14:36.840 --> 00:14:36.960
Okay.
好吧。

369
00:14:37.380 --> 00:14:45.600
Creed, per the script, is an amazing Joker from Batman, whereas Kevin is a, quote, lame Joker.
根据剧本，克里德是一个很棒的《蝙蝠侠》里的小丑，而凯文是一个“蹩脚的”小丑。

370
00:14:46.680 --> 00:14:49.880
And in the script it says, Dwight is also a Joker.
剧本里还写着，德怀特也是个小丑。

371
00:14:50.360 --> 00:14:52.740
Kelly is Carrie Bradshaw from Sex and the City.
凯莉是《欲望都市》里的凯莉·布雷德肖。

372
00:14:52.940 --> 00:14:55.340
Ryan is Gordon Gekko from Wall Street.
瑞安是《华尔街》里的戈登·盖柯。

373
00:14:55.780 --> 00:14:57.020
Very fitting for Ryan.
这很符合瑞安的风格。

374
00:14:57.780 --> 00:14:59.120
Oscar is Uncle Sam.
奥斯卡是山姆大叔。

375
00:14:59.340 --> 00:15:00.500
Meredith, a cheerleader.
梅雷迪斯是啦啦队长。

376
00:15:00.940 --> 00:15:02.320
Phyllis is Raggedy Ann.
菲利斯是布娃娃安妮。

377
00:15:02.960 --> 00:15:08.200
Andy, per the script, it says, he's dressed as a cat with whiskers on his face.
剧本里写着，安迪打扮成了一只脸上画着胡须的猫。

378
00:15:08.800 --> 00:15:10.940
Angela has brought back her cat costume.
安吉拉又穿回了她的猫咪装。

379
00:15:10.940 --> 00:15:12.140
Always a classic.
永远的经典。

380
00:15:12.560 --> 00:15:15.920
And Jim is just wearing a name tag that says, Dave.
吉姆只是戴了一个写着“戴夫”的名牌。

381
00:15:16.360 --> 00:15:22.060
And of course, Pam, the solo Halloween costume wearer at corporate is dressed as Charlie Chaplin.
当然，帕姆，作为公司里唯一穿万圣节服装的人，打扮成了查理·卓别林。

382
00:15:22.240 --> 00:15:22.640
Yes.
是的。

383
00:15:22.880 --> 00:15:26.160
I reached out to our wardrobe designer, Alicia Raycraft.
我联系了我们的服装设计师艾丽西亚·雷克拉夫特。

384
00:15:26.360 --> 00:15:27.060
Oh, great.
哦，太棒了。

385
00:15:27.360 --> 00:15:31.800
So starting this season, Alicia took over for Carrie Bennett.
从这一季开始，艾丽西亚接替了嘉莉·贝内特的工作。

386
00:15:32.360 --> 00:15:37.460
Alicia was amazing, particularly, I think, at building wardrobe from scratch.
艾丽西亚非常出色，尤其是在从零开始制作服装方面。

387
00:15:37.460 --> 00:15:47.260
My memories of her when I would visit her in the wardrobe trailer were that she always had, like, one of those fabric mannequins with, like, swatches on it, pinned on it,
我记得去服装拖车找她时，她总是有一个那种布艺人体模型，上面别着布料小样，

388
00:15:47.340 --> 00:15:48.200
or on her wall.
或者墙上贴着小样。

389
00:15:48.400 --> 00:15:51.240
I am telling you, she was always pinning something to something.
我跟你说，她总是在把什么东西别在什么东西上。

390
00:15:51.340 --> 00:15:51.560
Yes.
没错。

391
00:15:51.760 --> 00:15:53.440
And then standing back and looking at it.
然后退后一步审视它。

392
00:15:53.460 --> 00:15:53.560
Yes.
是的。

393
00:15:53.560 --> 00:15:55.680
And then moving a swatch here, up and down.
接着把小样移来移去，上上下下地调整。

394
00:15:55.680 --> 00:16:03.000
She said that with this episode, she had to really ride the line of designing wardrobe,
她说这一集她必须在设计服装的同时，

395
00:16:03.000 --> 00:16:08.020
but also making sure that the costumes looked like things that we could have put together ourselves.
还要确保这些服装看起来像是我们自己能拼凑出来的东西。

396
00:16:08.240 --> 00:16:08.520
Right.
没错。

397
00:16:08.640 --> 00:16:13.200
The idea is that if Kevin is going to dress like the Joker, it'd be Kevin's effort.
理念就是，如果凯文要打扮成小丑，那得是凯文自己努力的结果。

398
00:16:13.360 --> 00:16:15.360
It'd be, like, something Kevin had to put together.
得是那种凯文自己能凑出来的东西。

399
00:16:15.500 --> 00:16:15.940
Yes.
是的。

400
00:16:16.080 --> 00:16:21.480
Like you said, the script said that Creed's Joker was supposed to be the best version of the Joker.
就像你说的，剧本里写着克里德的小丑应该是最棒的小丑版本。

401
00:16:21.620 --> 00:16:23.120
Kevin's was supposed to be lame.
凯文的那套本该是很逊的。

402
00:16:23.300 --> 00:16:24.640
And they're the Dark Knight Joker.
而且他们扮的是《黑暗骑士》里的小丑。

403
00:16:24.640 --> 00:16:26.700
Yes, that's what Alicia said.
没错，艾丽西亚就是这么说的。

404
00:16:26.840 --> 00:16:30.600
They were supposed to be based on the Heath Ledger Joker.
他们本该是参考希斯·莱杰版小丑的。

405
00:16:30.980 --> 00:16:36.240
And so she had a picture, and she made a shopping list, and she still had her shopping liSt.
她当时有张照片，还列了购物清单，而且她还留着那份购物清单。

406
00:16:36.340 --> 00:16:36.960
Stop it.
别说了。

407
00:16:37.180 --> 00:16:38.100
I love her.
我爱死她了。

408
00:16:38.300 --> 00:16:39.400
This is what it said.
上面是这么写的。

409
00:16:39.740 --> 00:16:43.980
They had to go shop for a vest with a high neck center front.
他们得去买一件前领口很高的背心。

410
00:16:44.280 --> 00:16:46.660
Green for Creed, not for Kevin.
那是给克里德买的绿色，不是给凯文的。

411
00:16:46.920 --> 00:16:49.640
Because Creed got it right, and Kevin didn't.
因为克里德穿对了，而凯文穿错了。

412
00:16:49.780 --> 00:16:50.140
Correct.
没错。

413
00:16:50.520 --> 00:16:54.380
They needed a gray or dark lilac patterned shirt.
他们需要一件灰色或深紫色的花纹衬衫。

414
00:17:10.680 --> 00:17:18.380
She said the overall direction in shopping for Kevin was that all of the clothes they purchased should look like they came from his closet,
她说给凯文买衣服的总方针是，买来的所有衣服看起来都得像是他自己衣柜里有的，

415
00:17:18.380 --> 00:17:23.960
and the direction for Creed was that Creed went out and picked it out specifically for Halloween.
而给克里德的方针是，克里德是专门为了万圣节出去挑选的。

416
00:17:23.960 --> 00:17:24.540
Yeah.
是啊。

417
00:17:24.740 --> 00:17:30.420
But for Dwight, she said they went with a nod to the Jack Nicholson version of the Joker.
但对于德怀特，她说他们参考的是杰克·尼科尔森版的小丑。

418
00:17:30.420 --> 00:17:37.080
I thought something was different when I rewatched it, because the way they drew the smile did not look like the Heath Ledger Joker.
我重看的时候就觉得哪里不对劲，因为他们画的那个笑容看起来不像希斯·莱杰版的小丑。

419
00:17:37.400 --> 00:17:42.660
That's how they were like, how do we do three Jokers, but it's not all the same costume or the same look.
他们当时就在想，怎么才能做出三个小丑，但又不是完全一样的服装或造型。

420
00:17:42.820 --> 00:17:51.300
But she also shared with me that she brought in a rack of clothes and that Rain really put together his costume from everything she had bought,
但她还告诉我，她带了一衣架的衣服过去，雷恩确实是用她买的所有东西拼凑出了他的服装，

421
00:17:51.440 --> 00:17:53.940
which tracks with when we talked to Carrie.
这和我们之前采访凯莉时说的一致。

422
00:17:53.940 --> 00:17:58.480
And Carrie Bennett said that Rain was always really invested in what his character wore.
凯莉·贝内特说雷恩一直很在意他角色的穿着。

423
00:17:58.700 --> 00:17:59.540
That's awesome.
太棒了。

424
00:17:59.760 --> 00:18:01.160
So let's see, what's next?
那么，接下来是什么？

425
00:18:01.160 --> 00:18:04.500
We got a lot of questions about Andy's kitten costume.
我们收到了很多关于安迪小猫装扮的问题。

426
00:18:04.720 --> 00:18:05.100
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

427
00:18:05.600 --> 00:18:16.080
A lot of people wrote in to say they thought it looked a little bit like, my favorite was Katie L said, it looks like an off-brand Rum Tum Tugger costume from the musical Cats.
很多人写信来说他们觉得那看起来有点像，我最喜欢凯蒂·L说的，看起来像音乐剧《猫》里山寨版的“兰塔格”服装。

428
00:18:16.480 --> 00:18:21.860
She said, in my mind, I like to think Andy was in a school production of Cats and he still had his costume.
她说，在我看来，我觉得安迪当时参加了学校排演的《猫》，而且他还留着那套戏服。

429
00:18:22.920 --> 00:18:25.400
Katie L, you would be right on there.
凯蒂·L，你说得太对了。

430
00:18:25.400 --> 00:18:31.740
Dave told me that Greg was very involved in Ed's costume.
戴夫告诉我，格雷格非常关注埃德的服装。

431
00:18:32.240 --> 00:18:32.420
Really?
真的吗？

432
00:18:32.680 --> 00:18:39.960
Yes, that he wanted it to look like it was from the musical Cats and he went over the top to please Angela.
是的，他想让它看起来像是音乐剧《猫》里的，而且他为了讨好安吉拉，做得非常夸张。

433
00:18:40.220 --> 00:18:40.600
Right.
没错。

434
00:18:40.760 --> 00:18:43.320
He was not just going to draw whiskers on his face, guys.
伙计们，他可不只是要在脸上画几根胡须而已。

435
00:18:43.920 --> 00:18:53.200
Alicia said she showed Greg a bunch of photos from the Broadway musical of Cats and Greg picked his favorites, but she did not base this cat on any one character.
艾丽西亚说她给格雷格看了很多百老汇音乐剧《猫》的照片，格雷格挑了他最喜欢的，但她并没有让这只猫基于任何一个特定角色。

436
00:18:53.440 --> 00:18:54.200
It was a meld.
这是一个融合体。

437
00:18:54.380 --> 00:18:54.740
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

438
00:18:54.740 --> 00:18:56.900
She built that whole costume from scratch.
她是从零开始制作整套服装的。

439
00:18:57.080 --> 00:18:59.900
She bought a unitard and hand-painted it.
她买了一件连体紧身衣，然后手工上色。

440
00:19:00.120 --> 00:19:01.980
She used to do textile painting.
她以前做过纺织品绘画。

441
00:19:02.180 --> 00:19:02.380
Wow.
哇。

442
00:19:02.380 --> 00:19:03.760
I mean, that's amazing.
我是说，这太厉害了。

443
00:19:04.120 --> 00:19:07.400
And then she found another email that she shared with me.
然后她又找到了另一封邮件分享给我。

444
00:19:07.580 --> 00:19:15.800
It was an email to her crew detailing how to build the little, like, fur diaper thing that he's wearing.
那是一封发给她团队的邮件，详细说明了如何制作他穿的那个像毛绒尿布一样的东西。

445
00:19:16.020 --> 00:19:17.280
What is it, right?
那到底是什么，对吧？

446
00:19:17.620 --> 00:19:18.440
Yeah, I don't know.
是啊，我也不知道。

447
00:19:18.600 --> 00:19:20.360
It looks like fur underwear.
看起来像毛绒内裤。

448
00:19:20.540 --> 00:19:20.680
Yes.
没错。

449
00:19:20.680 --> 00:19:23.860
And then there's also, like, a rope belt and a tail and, oh, my goodness.
然后还有绳子腰带和尾巴，天哪。

450
00:19:23.860 --> 00:19:24.460
Yes.
是的。

451
00:19:24.680 --> 00:19:34.900
She said, please make a loincloth using a thong or small brief underwear as a base and then swatch Phelps, wool crepe, and heavy knits on top.
她说，请用丁字裤或小三角内裤做底，做一条缠腰带，然后在上面缝上菲尔普斯面料、羊毛绉纱和厚针织面料的布样。

452
00:19:35.060 --> 00:19:37.300
And please get faux fur for some gloves.
还要请你弄些人造毛皮来做手套。

453
00:19:40.160 --> 00:19:41.080
So amazing.
太棒了。

454
00:19:41.300 --> 00:19:46.520
So that is how she put together all of those costumes, which were really amazing.
所以她就是这样把那些服装拼凑起来的，真的很厉害。

455
00:19:46.660 --> 00:19:47.900
And I remember my costume.
我还记得我的戏服。

456
00:19:48.300 --> 00:19:52.200
We did, like, Pam went to a store and rented a tux, basically.
我们当时，就像，帕姆去店里租了一套燕尾服，基本上就是这样。

457
00:19:52.200 --> 00:19:54.320
Well, I took a lot of photos this day.
嗯，那天我拍了很多照片。

458
00:19:54.500 --> 00:19:56.180
I have some great ones of you and Rain.
我拍了一些你和雷恩的很棒的照片。

459
00:19:56.380 --> 00:19:57.960
You guys were hanging out by your trailer.
你们当时在你们的拖车旁闲逛。

460
00:19:58.200 --> 00:20:07.360
I was walking by you guys in my cat costume, and I see Rain as the Joker talking to Jenna as Charlie Chaplin, just casually hanging out.
我穿着猫咪装从你们身边走过，看到雷恩扮成小丑，正和扮成查理·卓别林的珍娜聊天，就像平常闲聊一样。

461
00:20:07.900 --> 00:20:09.320
And so I took pictures.
所以我拍了照片。

462
00:20:09.500 --> 00:20:10.520
They're some of my favorite.
那是我最喜欢的几张照片之一。

463
00:20:10.780 --> 00:20:12.540
Well, I think he put that one in his book.
嗯，我想他把那张照片放进他的书里了。

464
00:20:12.740 --> 00:20:13.640
I gave it to him.
是我给他的。

465
00:20:13.680 --> 00:20:13.900
Yeah.
是啊。

466
00:20:13.980 --> 00:20:14.600
That's from me.
那是我给他的。

467
00:20:14.600 --> 00:20:24.160
I loved this episode, Angela, because I had been away for a very long time at Pratt, but, you know, the corporate offices were over on the warehouse set.
安吉拉，我很喜欢这一集，因为我当时在普拉特待了很长一段时间，但你知道，公司办公室是在仓库布景那边。

468
00:20:24.280 --> 00:20:25.320
We never got to see you.
我们从来没机会见到你。

469
00:20:25.420 --> 00:20:26.840
But you did on this day.
但那天你见到了。

470
00:20:27.120 --> 00:20:27.520
Exactly.
没错。

471
00:20:27.760 --> 00:20:33.120
And I got to participate in the Halloween, which was always one of my favorite things on our show.
而且我能参与万圣节活动，这一直是我在剧中最喜欢的事情之一。

472
00:20:33.440 --> 00:20:38.800
And I would have been really bummed if I didn't get to see everybody in their costumes, but I got to be in hair makeup.
如果没能看到大家穿戏服的样子，我会非常沮丧的，但我有机会去化妆间了。

473
00:20:39.040 --> 00:20:40.580
And we were in there a long time.
我们在里面待了很久。

474
00:20:40.740 --> 00:20:43.920
Me, not so long, but, oh, my gosh, Ed had to come in really early.
我倒还好，没待太久，但天哪，艾德必须来得非常早。

475
00:20:44.080 --> 00:20:44.360
Yeah.
是啊。

476
00:20:44.600 --> 00:20:45.780
And so did Phyllis.
菲利斯也是。

477
00:20:45.960 --> 00:20:47.320
Like, there was a lot of makeup there.
那里的妆容真的很复杂。

478
00:20:47.580 --> 00:20:50.420
Well, my hair was not easy to wash out, I'll tell you that.
说真的，我的头发可没那么容易洗干净。

479
00:20:50.620 --> 00:20:51.540
Are your eyebrows.
还有你的眉毛。

480
00:20:51.540 --> 00:20:53.340
I felt bad for your poor eyebrows.
我真为你的眉毛感到难过。

481
00:20:53.700 --> 00:20:55.840
It was a real grease paint.
那可是真正的油彩。

482
00:20:56.080 --> 00:20:57.140
They shellacked you.
他们给你涂了厚厚一层。

483
00:20:57.320 --> 00:20:57.620
Yeah.
是啊。

484
00:20:57.880 --> 00:21:00.820
I have a few little background catches for this cold open.
关于这个开场戏，我还有几个小花絮。

485
00:21:01.000 --> 00:21:10.280
I want you guys to know that at 44 seconds, when Kevin is annoyed that Creed is such a good joker, he brushes past me and knocks me over.
我想让你们知道，在44秒的时候，当凯文因为克里德扮的小丑太像而感到恼火时，他从我身边擦过，把我撞倒了。

486
00:21:10.280 --> 00:21:15.860
This was like a little running bit Brian and I would have that if Kevin bumped into Angela, she'd go flying.
这就像是布莱恩和我之间的一个小梗，如果凯文撞到安吉拉，她就会飞出去。

487
00:21:15.860 --> 00:21:18.900
It was like our own personal bit that cracked us up to no end.
这是我们私人的小梗，每次都把我们逗得不行。

488
00:21:19.220 --> 00:21:23.740
When he did it, one of my cat ears fell forward and didn't come back up.
当他撞我的时候，我的一只猫耳朵耷拉下来，没能弹回去。

489
00:21:23.740 --> 00:21:26.620
And I could feel it laying on top of my head.
我能感觉到它趴在我的头顶上。

490
00:21:26.720 --> 00:21:28.160
And I was trying not to laugh.
我当时努力忍住不笑。

491
00:21:28.280 --> 00:21:31.620
And if you go to 44 seconds, you'll see that Angela's ear flops forward.
如果你去看44秒，你会看到安吉拉的耳朵耷拉下来了。

492
00:21:32.000 --> 00:21:37.420
I want you to know that three people that I reached out to on this episode pointed out that moment to me.
我想让你知道，有三个人在这一集播出后专门向我指出了那个瞬间。

493
00:21:37.420 --> 00:21:37.980
I know.
我知道。

494
00:21:38.280 --> 00:21:38.820
I know.
我知道。

495
00:21:38.880 --> 00:21:40.380
They talked about it in the commentary, too.
他们在评论音轨里也提到了这件事。

496
00:21:40.500 --> 00:21:43.060
I think it's gone down in the lore of this episode.
我想这已经成了这一集的传说之一了。

497
00:21:43.220 --> 00:21:43.640
I know.
我知道。

498
00:21:43.840 --> 00:21:49.800
And then the other thing was, you guys, they really let Ed as that cat play around and mess with John.
还有一件事，伙计们，他们真的让艾德扮成那只猫，四处走动，去逗约翰。

499
00:21:50.020 --> 00:21:57.520
And in one take, Ed as Andy came up to Jim and rubbed on his leg, like kind of rubbed on him like a cat.
有一次拍摄时，艾德扮的安迪走到吉姆身边，在他的腿上蹭了蹭，就像猫一样蹭他。

500
00:21:57.800 --> 00:21:59.640
And the two of them lost it.
结果他们两个都笑场了。

501
00:21:59.760 --> 00:22:00.600
It's in the bloopers.
那是在花絮里。

502
00:22:00.760 --> 00:22:02.440
But they had a lot of fun with that.
但他们拍那段拍得很开心。

503
00:22:02.440 --> 00:22:09.540
One of my favorite moments is when Andy, it says in the script, Andy walks back to his desk smugly.
我最喜欢的时刻之一是安迪，剧本上写着，安迪得意洋洋地走回他的办公桌。

504
00:22:10.460 --> 00:22:14.520
And Ed's like sashay in that cat costume cracked me up.
艾德穿着那身猫咪装扭着腰走过来，真的把我逗乐了。

505
00:22:14.880 --> 00:22:19.620
You guys know we love this fake elevator in our lobby, the Dunder Mifflin lobby.
你们知道我们很喜欢大厅里的那个假电梯，邓德·米夫林大厅里的那个。

506
00:22:20.000 --> 00:22:20.320
Yeah.
没错。

507
00:22:20.400 --> 00:22:21.100
We've talked about it.
我们聊过这个。

508
00:22:21.200 --> 00:22:22.900
Two wooden doors and a guy pulling a rope.
两扇木门，还有个人在旁边拉绳子。

509
00:22:23.120 --> 00:22:23.320
Yep.
是的。

510
00:22:23.520 --> 00:22:24.140
On the side.
在旁边。

511
00:22:24.320 --> 00:22:25.720
And they add all the sound effects later.
他们后来会加上所有的音效。

512
00:22:26.020 --> 00:22:26.520
They add it all in.
全都加进去。

513
00:22:26.520 --> 00:22:33.160
And well, in the script, when Rain as Dwight arrives in the Joker outfit, he just was supposed to hop in the elevator.
嗯，剧本里，当雷恩饰演的德怀特穿着小丑装到达时，他本该直接跳进电梯。

514
00:22:33.360 --> 00:22:37.520
And he was supposed to, a la the Joker, say, and here we go.
他本该模仿小丑说，我们要开始了。

515
00:22:37.560 --> 00:22:38.840
And the doors would shut.
然后门会关上。

516
00:22:38.980 --> 00:22:39.220
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

517
00:22:39.360 --> 00:22:40.860
But it was just kind of falling flat.
但效果有点平淡。

518
00:22:40.920 --> 00:22:44.560
So they came up with this alt about the magic trick of the pencil disappearing.
所以他们想出了一个替代方案，关于铅笔消失的魔术。

519
00:22:44.740 --> 00:22:44.860
Yeah.
对。

520
00:22:45.000 --> 00:22:46.860
And it wasn't really working still.
但还是不太行。

521
00:22:47.080 --> 00:22:52.060
And so Anthony pitched, what if the doors close as he's saying the line?
于是安东尼提议，如果他在说台词时门关上了会怎样？

522
00:22:52.400 --> 00:22:55.080
And then he opens them back up to finish the sentence.
然后他再把门打开把话说完。

523
00:22:55.080 --> 00:22:59.160
And they said they played around with this for a bit, with the doors opening and closing,
他们说他们在那儿折腾了一会儿，开关门，

524
00:22:59.320 --> 00:23:03.880
which you and I know means that there was someone working that pulley really hard.
你我都知道这意味着有人在拼命拉那个滑轮。

525
00:23:04.060 --> 00:23:05.620
And that's how they found this moment.
他们就是这样发现了这个瞬间。

526
00:23:05.620 --> 00:23:07.080
And I thought that was really fun.
我觉得这真的很有趣。

527
00:23:07.240 --> 00:23:08.160
That is awesome.
太棒了。

528
00:23:08.520 --> 00:23:12.480
Those things that happened on the fly like that in the moment, I love to hear about.
我特别喜欢听这种在现场即兴发挥出来的东西。

529
00:23:12.880 --> 00:23:14.940
Now it's time to get into the episode.
现在是时候进入剧集了。

530
00:23:15.280 --> 00:23:16.560
We're down in the warehouse.
我们在仓库里。

531
00:23:16.660 --> 00:23:21.900
They are loading up a big truck so that they can take Holly to Nashua.
他们正在装一辆大卡车，这样他们就能把霍莉带去纳舒厄。

532
00:23:22.140 --> 00:23:22.580
Yes.
是的。

533
00:23:22.960 --> 00:23:24.440
We got a fan question.
我们有一个粉丝提问。

534
00:23:24.440 --> 00:23:25.060
Okay.
好的。

535
00:23:25.440 --> 00:23:27.340
That is very funny to me.
我觉得这很有趣。

536
00:23:27.800 --> 00:23:28.440
Two people.
两个人。

537
00:23:28.860 --> 00:23:29.080
Okay.
好的。

538
00:23:29.460 --> 00:23:30.120
Ian O.
伊恩·O。

539
00:23:30.340 --> 00:23:31.120
and Mary S.
和玛丽·S。

540
00:23:31.340 --> 00:23:32.120
wrote in to say,
写信来说，

541
00:23:32.320 --> 00:23:35.340
did Holly live in the warehouse?
霍莉是住在仓库里吗？

542
00:23:36.740 --> 00:23:42.060
Isn't it odd that this road trip started from the office rather than from her home?
这次公路旅行从办公室出发而不是从她家出发，这不奇怪吗？

543
00:23:42.240 --> 00:23:44.940
This is such a good catch.
这真是个好问题。

544
00:23:45.240 --> 00:23:48.360
Is this stuff coming from?
这些东西是从哪儿来的？

545
00:23:49.320 --> 00:23:50.260
Oh my gosh.
天哪。

546
00:23:50.380 --> 00:23:54.480
I guess we have to justify it that they went to her apartment, packed it up, but then why
我想我们得解释说他们去了她的公寓，打包好了，但为什么

547
00:23:54.480 --> 00:23:55.940
did they drive to the warehouse?
他们要开车去仓库？

548
00:23:56.020 --> 00:23:57.380
Why not just leave?
为什么不直接出发？

549
00:23:58.180 --> 00:24:03.080
This piggybacks very nicely on a question that I had along with Aaron S.
这和我以及亚伦·S。

550
00:24:03.220 --> 00:24:03.880
and Amanda E.
还有阿曼达·E提出的问题衔接得非常好。

551
00:24:03.880 --> 00:24:07.160
What is Holly wearing on the day she is moving?
霍莉搬家那天穿的是什么？

552
00:24:07.400 --> 00:24:11.260
She is dressed in her work clothes, same as Pam driving to Pratt.
她穿着工作服，就像帕姆开车去普拉特学院时穿的那样。

553
00:24:11.340 --> 00:24:11.820
I know.
我知道。

554
00:24:12.080 --> 00:24:12.840
What is that?
那是什么？

555
00:24:13.080 --> 00:24:14.180
Michael's more casual.
迈克尔穿得更休闲。

556
00:24:14.520 --> 00:24:17.360
He's got his little casual little like zippy jacket.
他穿着那件带拉链的小休闲夹克。

557
00:24:17.660 --> 00:24:17.940
Yes.
没错。

558
00:24:17.940 --> 00:24:23.720
Also, they pointed out, I don't think it looks like she had any intention of helping move
而且他们指出，我觉得她看起来根本没打算帮忙搬运

559
00:24:23.720 --> 00:24:24.940
any of her own belongings.
她自己的任何行李。

560
00:24:25.060 --> 00:24:26.700
She is not dressed for a move.
她穿的衣服根本不适合搬家。

561
00:24:26.920 --> 00:24:27.400
No.
没错。

562
00:24:27.620 --> 00:24:28.380
She's not.
确实不是。

563
00:24:28.660 --> 00:24:29.840
Why could she be casual?
她为什么穿得那么休闲？

564
00:24:29.840 --> 00:24:30.560
What's happening?
发生了什么？

565
00:24:30.740 --> 00:24:32.240
I thought these were good catches.
我觉得这些细节抓得很好。

566
00:24:32.580 --> 00:24:36.980
You know, I talked to Dave about this, and he said that during the prep for this episode,
你知道吗，我和戴夫聊过这件事，他说在筹备这一集时，

567
00:24:37.180 --> 00:24:44.820
they brought him a bunch of trucks to look at, and they were all giant 18-wheeler moving
他们带了一堆卡车让他看，全都是巨大的18轮搬家

568
00:24:44.820 --> 00:24:48.980
trucks, and he was like, how am I going to film with that?
卡车，他当时就想，我该怎么拍这些大家伙？

569
00:24:49.080 --> 00:24:50.140
How do I tow it?
我怎么拖动它？

570
00:24:50.340 --> 00:24:51.280
What am I doing?
我该怎么办？

571
00:24:51.780 --> 00:24:54.620
But he said he loves this truck that they found.
但他后来说他很喜欢他们找到的这辆卡车。

572
00:24:54.840 --> 00:24:55.880
It looked really realistic.
看起来非常真实。

573
00:24:55.880 --> 00:25:01.260
He also just loved that the back was open, because then when you got shots that, you know,
他还特别喜欢车厢后部是敞开的设计，因为这样当你拍摄那些，你知道的，

574
00:25:01.340 --> 00:25:06.620
the farther shots of them going down the road, it just like, you really felt the move.
他们在路上行驶的远景镜头时，你真的能感觉到搬家的氛围。

575
00:25:06.800 --> 00:25:07.100
Yeah.
是啊。

576
00:25:07.100 --> 00:25:08.500
Because you could see her bed.
因为你能看到她的床。

577
00:25:08.500 --> 00:25:09.700
You could see the stuff.
你能看到那些东西。

578
00:25:09.960 --> 00:25:10.140
Right.
没错。

579
00:25:10.240 --> 00:25:14.020
They said that they wanted the table hanging off the front, like in the bubble wrap.
他们说他们想让桌子挂在前面，就像用气泡膜包着那样。

580
00:25:14.020 --> 00:25:14.920
I love it.
我喜欢这个设计。

581
00:25:15.080 --> 00:25:15.820
I loved it, too.
我也很喜欢。

582
00:25:16.100 --> 00:25:18.500
Phil Props, you know, we love Phil Props.
道具师菲尔，你知道的，我们都很喜欢道具师菲尔。

583
00:25:18.620 --> 00:25:23.440
He shared that Anthony and Dave really wanted Michael to have packed all kinds of crazy things
他分享说安东尼和戴夫真的很想让迈克尔在公路旅行中

584
00:25:23.440 --> 00:25:24.160
for the road trip.
打包各种疯狂的东西。

585
00:25:24.300 --> 00:25:28.020
Like him and Holly are little kids, like the finger puppets and the cats in the cradle
就像他和霍莉是小孩子一样，比如手指木偶、翻绳游戏

586
00:25:28.020 --> 00:25:29.660
and the movies to watch.
还有要看的电影。

587
00:25:29.800 --> 00:25:32.380
You guys, a lot of those are in the deleted scenes.
伙计们，其中很多都在删减片段里。

588
00:25:32.660 --> 00:25:33.040
Aw.
啊。

589
00:25:33.200 --> 00:25:35.100
Of them doing it in the van?
是他们在货车里做这些事的片段吗？

590
00:25:35.360 --> 00:25:38.180
And my absolute favorite is the two of them.
我最喜欢的是他们两个的那一段。

591
00:25:38.360 --> 00:25:43.200
The windows are down, and they're watching a movie, and they are pissing themselves laughing.
车窗摇下来，他们在看电影，笑得前仰后合。

592
00:25:43.200 --> 00:25:49.280
They are laughing so hard, and Daryl looks miserable, and Daryl takes a hard turn on purpose,
他们笑得太厉害了，达里尔看起来很痛苦，于是达里尔故意猛地转弯，

593
00:25:49.420 --> 00:25:52.760
and the laptop that's playing the movie goes flying out the window.
播放电影的笔记本电脑就直接飞出了窗外。

594
00:25:53.160 --> 00:25:54.700
I remember that.
我记得那个片段。

595
00:25:54.900 --> 00:25:56.040
It is so funny.
太搞笑了。

596
00:25:56.180 --> 00:25:57.920
I am so bummed it didn't make it in.
没能放进正片里我真的好难过。

597
00:25:58.560 --> 00:26:03.120
Dave said they spent three hours on that gag and finally had to just let it go.
戴夫说他们为了这个笑点花了三个小时，最后不得不放弃了。

598
00:26:03.360 --> 00:26:07.740
They said every time Craig turned, the computer would slide and never go out the window.
他们说每次克雷格转弯时，电脑都会滑开，就是飞不出窗外。

599
00:26:07.740 --> 00:26:10.920
It only went out the window one time.
它只飞出窗外过一次。

600
00:26:11.280 --> 00:26:12.360
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

601
00:26:12.360 --> 00:26:15.500
But it's in the bloopers on the DVD, and it's so funny.
但它在DVD的NG花絮里，真的太搞笑了。

602
00:26:15.780 --> 00:26:19.940
We had a fan catch from a couple of people, from Erica S.
有几位粉丝发现了这一点，Erica S.和Mary S.，

603
00:26:20.020 --> 00:26:22.260
and Mary S., and I have to say
我得说，

604
00:26:22.260 --> 00:26:24.000
they're making a good point.
她们说得很有道理。

605
00:26:24.340 --> 00:26:24.760
What?
什么？

606
00:26:24.760 --> 00:26:32.680
So it's said repeatedly in Goodbye, Toby that, you know, she's coming in to train for this
在《再见，托比》里反复提到，你知道，她来这里是为了接受这个

607
00:26:32.680 --> 00:26:36.940
new position, and that they only allowed one day for training.
新职位的培训，而且他们只给了一天的培训时间。

608
00:26:37.260 --> 00:26:42.600
And when she's on the Ferris wheel with Michael, she talks about how she was unable to be promoted
当她和迈克尔坐摩天轮时，她谈到自己无法在

609
00:26:42.600 --> 00:26:44.180
at her former company.
前公司获得晋升。

610
00:26:44.720 --> 00:26:45.760
Former company.
前公司。

611
00:26:45.860 --> 00:26:46.200
Right, right.
对，没错。

612
00:26:46.200 --> 00:26:52.660
But then in this episode, it says she's being transferred back to Nashua, as if she's been
但在这集里，却说她要被调回纳舒厄，就好像她一直以来

613
00:26:52.660 --> 00:26:54.680
a Dunder Mifflin employee all along.
都是邓德·米夫林的员工一样。

614
00:26:54.860 --> 00:26:56.220
I don't know, guys.
我不知道，伙计们。

615
00:26:56.420 --> 00:26:58.900
I mean, I think they caught a continuity error there.
我是说，我觉得她们发现了一个连续性错误。

616
